        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54e128b8-1d25-53c7-91cc-42ae8432e255",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Quagmire, Seth MacFarlane, Brian Griffin, Cheryl Tiegs\n- Works: Family Guy, Ted, Ted 2, A Million Ways to Die in the West, Tiegs for Two\n- Topics: character portrayal, film roles, episode plot\n\nFacts:\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted\" in 2012.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"A Million Ways to Die in the West\" in 2014.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted 2\" in 2015.\n- Seth MacFarlane, the creator and voice actor of Glenn Quagmire on Family Guy, described Quagmire as \"an appalling human being who is still caught in the rat-pack era\" and based on anachronistic 1950s party-animal clichés.\n- In the Family Guy episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Brian Griffin fails again at getting a date and seeks advice from his sex-crazed neighbor Glenn Quagmire.\n- In \"Tiegs for Two,\" Glenn Quagmire is also pursuing his ex-lover, actress Cheryl Tiegs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
